  "problem": "Concurrent enrichment jobs could silently exceed the selected spend cap. Missing prices could be treated as free. Interrupted provider responses could be assumed uncharged. Unchanged reruns could repurchase the same task. Pilot $10 / monthly $50 values could be hidden defaults. Cost reports could omit failures, retries and rejected proposals.",
  "resulting_behavior": "createBudgetLedger reserves worst-case spend from input tokens, max output/reasoning tokens, selected maximum prices and retry policy using an exclusive atomic queue. Two workers racing for the final budget unit cannot both proceed. Missing price data fails closed. settle persists usage/cost/provider IDs on success and uncertain-charge state on timeout-after-send, malformed usage and process restart; uncertain charges are not assumed free. 429 honors Retry-After and is retry-capped; 402 is payment_required. createJobCache keys proposals by source bytes, parser/prompt/schema/model/provider-policy versions and task scope. A changed source or prompt invalidates the cache; an unchanged rerun performs no duplicate inference. Suggested $10 pilot / $50 monthly values are editable configuration with hidden_default=false. The cost report includes failures, retries and rejected proposals. Paid calls remain disabled.",
